                     sys.mine.none.txt: same with --xt=none.
    jobs.txt         abseil 20240722 (163 TUs) + fmt 11.0.2 in configs A-J (obj/<cfg>.*.o):
                     A gcc-a64 -O2 -fPIC; B gcc-a64 -O3 -fpic -fno-semantic-interposition;
                     C gcc-x64 -O2 -fPIC; D clang22-a64 -O2 -fPIC -fno-sem-int; E clang19-x64 -Os -fPIC;
                     F gcc-a64 -O2 -fPIE (the non-PIC twin of A).  Run: xargs -P4 -d'\n' -n1 sh -c < jobs.txt
    jobs2.txt        arpack-ng 3.9.1 gfortran P=-fPIC / Q=-fPIE (objf/).
    bb-pic/ bb-pie/  busybox 1.36.1 defconfig, CFLAGS -fPIC / -fPIE (make -j4 in each; *.lst = object lists).
    cx/              c1.cc, c2.c constructed idioms (arrays to their end, static members, inline vars,
                     constexpr tables beside exported globals) x gcc/clang19/clang22/x86 gcc/clang x86
                     x O0..Os x 8 flag sets; cx.mine.txt / cx.author.txt.
                     Boundary false refusal: cx/c2.clang22-O2-fPIC.o (AArch64, `static int arr[10]; int after;`).
    xt/              x1-x4.c x86 t-clause cases, built as xt/xN.<compiler>-<O>.o with -fPIC.
                     python3 rule.py --hits xt/x4.x86_64-linux-gnu-gcc-O2.o -> refused
                     (movl $99999,sz(%rip) named as exported gz); python3 xamb.py xt/*.o
  xamb.py            checks the x86 `+4+t` clause against the true instruction end (objdump -dw):
                     python3 xamb.py FILES...  -> WRONG/ok per t-sensitive use, TOTAL line.
                     real false refusal: python3 xamb.py obj/C.abseil-cpp-20240722.0_absl_time_format.cc.o
